 part  of who's the next person you see as an  analyst  an in-game analyst who's going to be  successful you know you bring up a good  point because  i think to your point we see brees sort  of talking off the cuff as he did with  the anthem situation  and how much it got him in trouble and i  i don't know if that makes you a little  bit more gun shy to sort of feel like  you can  put your opinion out there because you  see how quickly  there can be a backlash and and that  applies to your football take  that can apply to your political take  and some people  are capable of sort of going out there  and again i think there has to be an ego  and a narcissism behind it where you are  so  confident in what you're saying you're  not afraid of defending your position  so i i've always thought drew is sort of  the interesting one like i've  i love peyton manning peyton manning i  mean we even just saw that when  they did the golf tournament he's just  so good off the cuff  it's natural it's not contrived i think  cam jordan  if you're gonna look to the saints  locker room i've done  uh red carpet with him for nfl honors  he's amazing he's done a lot of this  stuff too  off to the side just on the ig story so  he's done a lot of stuff with us  i think he's studio though i think he's  studio jane  i think i think cam because you get more  opportunities there  and you you can tell stories there it's  hard to tell a story in a game  and i think cam has that personality i  want to see that personality too  i think phillip rivers might be sneaky  great in the booth i love philip reverse  i would love you know it's funny i  haven't actually heard his name really  tossed out there that much  he is so fun to watch even just has his  impassioned speech  leaving the chargers right uh i have so  much disrespect for him just as a human  when we did the pro bowl uh his  daughters had a daddy-daughter dance  and he flew all the way from orlando  back to san diego and then back again  for